   "properties": {
    "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
    "ver": "0.35.0",
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Comfy UGC - 3 Speech take with voice reference\n\n**Speech take with voice reference** (7.3 s): same as a speech take, plus the voice of this speaker's first take as <Audio 1> so the voice stays the same and the packshot as <Picture 1>. Model: ref2va (reference model: packshot and/or voice references; stills pinned with Add Guide). Speed: 8-step turbo LoRA.\n\n**Take 3 of the spec**\n1. \"This is the one I actually kept taking.\"\n2. \"Here is what is on the label.\"\n\n**How to use**\n1. Make the stills first (**1 Keyframe stills**) and set them on **FIRST FRAME** and **LAST FRAME** (the preloaded ones are samples). Every object the take moves must be visible and within reach in the first frame.\n2. **Audio 1**: the voice of this speaker's first take: `ffmpeg -i <first take>.mp4 -vn -ac 1 -ar 24000 -c:a pcm_s16le voice.wav`.\n3. Group 1: **HQ?** on (default) = HQ 768x1376, the approved look (a 15 s speech take is about $0.44); off = draft 576x1024 for quick tests.\n4. Group 0: the **PROMPT** comes from `take_graph.py --print-prompt` (MiniMax's own caption format). Edit it in the same style: describe only what is seen and heard, no negations ('nothing floats' makes things float), spoken words only inside `<d>[English] ...</d>` after `(S1)`. Change **SEED** to re-roll.\n5. Run, then check it with **5 Review (Gemini QA)** and by eye and ear.\n\n**Preloaded**: take 3 prompt, seed, sample stills, size (576x1024 draft / 768x1376 HQ), length 175 frames (17k+5 grid at 24 fps).\n\n**Turbo LoRA**: `lightx2v__Minimax-h3-Turbo__minimax_h3_ref2v_turbo_8step_v1.0_768p_comfyui_bf16.safetensors` (import it from huggingface.co/lightx2v/Minimax-h3-Turbo into your models first)\n\n**Not in this workflow (runs locally in the skill)**\nSpend guard, the lint (`take_graph.py --lint`), upload of stills and downloading the file: `take_graph.py --submit` does them. In the UI you press Run yourself (it costs credits).\n\nSource: `scripts/ui_build.py` in the repo. Edit here in the UI, then run `scripts/ui_sync.py pull \"<name>\"` and the agent updates the skill to match."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
 ],
